Aim

To implement a complete CI/CD pipeline using GitHub, Jenkins, testing, Docker build, and container execution.

Theory (Short)

CI/CD pipeline automates software development workflow.
GitHub stores code, Jenkins builds and tests it, Docker creates containers, and the application runs automatically.
This ensures continuous integration and continuous deployment.

Steps
Step 1: Push Project to GitHub
git init
git add .
git commit -m "CI/CD Pipeline"
git remote add origin https://github.com/username/lab20.git
git push -u origin main
Step 2: Create Dockerfile
FROM openjdk:17
COPY . /app
WORKDIR /app
RUN javac Hello.java
CMD ["java", "Hello"]
Step 3: Create Jenkinsfile
pipeline {
    agent any

    stages {

        stage('Checkout') {
            steps {
                git 'https://github.com/username/lab20.git'
            }
        }

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                bat 'mvn clean test'
            }
        }

        stage('Docker Build') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker build -t cicd-app .'
            }
        }

        stage('Run Container') {
            steps {
                bat 'docker run cicd-app'
            }
        }
    }
}
Step 4: Run Jenkins Pipeline
Build Now

Pipeline Flow:

GitHub → Jenkins → Maven Test → Docker Build → Run Container
Result

End-to-end CI/CD pipeline was successfully implemented using GitHub, Jenkins, and Docker.

Outcome

Complete CI/CD workflow experience was achieved.
